{"id":"src/lib/pdf/edsPdfDocument.tsx","pkg":"src/lib/pdf","kind":"ui","lines":483,"commentLines":28,"header":["THE PAINTER of the EDS PDF: takes the document model (edsPdfModel.ts) and lays it out on A4 pages with @react-pdf/renderer. It decides nothing about the content. It is loaded only when someone clicks \"Download PDF\" (the library is large). I make every block that must stay whole (a finding, a chart card, a table row) unbreakable, so a page never cuts one in half; a long table continues on the next page."],"symbols":[{"name":"BODY_LINE_HEIGHT","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":14,"sig":"const BODY_LINE_HEIGHT = 1.45","type":"","doc":["I set the body line height (1.45) on EVERY text, not on the page and not on a wrapper: a page-level line height makes the library drop the footer's \"Page x of y\" (and the whole footer), and a line height inherited through a wrapper View is applied wider than 1.45 (the question, the table headings and the sources came out spaced out, and the section bars sat below their headings). A style given to a text overrides this one. EXCEPT the footer's page number: a text with a `render` function and ANY line height is dropped by the library, so that one uses the library's own Text, with none."],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"e0e08bf188-BODY_LINE_HEIGHT","usedBy":[]},{"name":"Text","kind":"component","exported":false,"line":15,"async":false,"sig":"const Text = ({ style, ...rest }: any) =>","params":[{"name":"{ style, ...rest }","type":"any","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""}],"returns":"","doc":[],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"e0e08bf188-Text","usedBy":[]},{"name":"C","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":17,"sig":"const C = { ink: \"#0f172a\", text: \"#1e293b\", body: \"#334155\", muted: \"#64748b\", faint: \"#94a3b8\", rule: \"#e2e8f0\", s …","type":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"key","name":"ink","line":18,"value":"\"#0f172a\"","doc":[]},{"kind":"key","name":"text","line":19,"value":"\"#1e293b\"","doc":[]},{"